{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_011Cg2pFxBaPFsTLpqSfSWvK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a full picture. Let me analyze what needs to be done:\n\n1. **storage/storage.go** needs to:\n   - Add context.Context support (already has it partially)\n   - `Put` must reject a canceled context without mutation\n   - Revision conflict handling (CAS - compare-and-swap): reject if existing revision != expected\n   - Snapshot independence (return a copy, not the underlying map)\n   - Concurrency safety (use sync.RWMutex)\n   - Validate inputs: empty key, negative revision\n\n2. **api/api.go** needs to:\n   - `Update` signature needs to keep existing external API (no context), but call the new storage Put with context\n   - It should still accept the same parameters, but internally pass context.Background() when calling storage.Put\n\n3. **export/export.go** and **replica/replica.go** keep their existing signatures unchanged, but since `Snapshot()` now requires a context argument, both call sites need to pass context.Background() internally.\n\nNow I'm walking through the test expectations: TestCAS verifies that a successful put with revision 0 succeeds, a stale put with the same expected revision fails, empty keys and negative revisions are rejected, and snapshots are independent copies that don't alias the underlying store data. Then I'm moving into checking what TestConcurrent expects around simultaneous access.\n\nNow I need to figure out the actual implementation changes: storage.go needs a mutex for concurrency, with Put checking context cancellation, validating the key and expected revision, enforcing CAS semantics (only succeeding when the existing revision matches expected), and Snapshot returning a safe copy of the map. Tracing through TestCAS confirms the expected behavior: the first Put with expected=0 succeeds and sets Revision=1, while a second Put with the same expected=0 should fail since the revision has already moved forward.\n\nWriting store struct and constructor...\n\nAdding Get and Snapshot methods...\n\nNow I'm wiring up the API layer to keep the existing Update signature while threading context.Background() into the storage call, then starting on an export package that serializes the store state to JSON.\n\nSince Snapshot now returns a true copy instead of aliasing the internal map, I'm fixing replica.Copy to rely on that copy so mutations to the replica don't leak back into the original store, which is exactly what the aliasing test checks for.\n\nLooking at TestConcurrent next, it spins up 20 goroutines all calling Put with the same key and expected revision 0, then checks the final revision equals 1 -- confirming CAS semantics mean only the first write wins while the rest fail against the now-nonzero revision.\n\nNow I'm ready to write out all the files.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1086,"cache_read_input_tokens":16100,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1086,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7e213a2c-fddb-424b-a79a-e7d0c695ea36","uuid":"86391278-3899-4c51-aaa7-d98a8dd539e7"}
